---
// The same page in Dutch is ../index.astro; change them together.
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro"
import About from "../../components/About.astro"
import Case from "../../components/Case.astro"
import Cases from "../../components/Cases.astro"
import Contact from "../../components/Contact.astro"
import Container from "../../components/Container.astro"
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro"
import Main from "../../components/Main.astro"
import { UI } from "../../data/ui"

import hogeschoolUtrecht from "../../images/hogeschool-utrecht.png"
import nerds from "../../images/nerds.png"
import nexusInstituut from "../../images/nexus-instituut.png"
import quaiDesNotaires from "../../images/quai-des-notaires.png"
import speld from "../../images/speld.png"

import IconDesign from "../../svgs/feature_design.svg"
import IconBuild from "../../svgs/feature_build.svg"
import IconService from "../../svgs/feature_service.svg"
---

<Base description={UI.en.description} lang="en" alternate="/">
  <Header />
  <Main>
    <About>
      <h1>Stef Thoen</h1>
      <p>
        I'm a freelance full-stack developer with a background in Computer
        Science and Philosophy. I work from France for Dutch clients.
      </p>
    </About>
    <Container>
      <section class="story">
        <p>
          In October 2013 I set off with my wife and{" "}
          <a href="http://joepdezoeperd.nl">Joep de Zoeperd</a> to roam Europe
          as a digital nomad.
        </p>
        <p>
          We got stranded in the Morvan in France, where we lived in a{" "}
          <a href="https://www.paprikapatterns.com/building-home-mounting-yurt/">
            yurt
          </a>{" "}
          for two years. In the summer of 2017 we{" "}
          <a href="http://peuapeu.nl">
            bought an old farmhouse that we're renovating
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="features">
        <h2>What do I do?</h2>
        <div>
          <article>
            <IconDesign class="icon" />
            <h3>Design</h3>
            <p>
              I research, sketch and build prototypes. I make sure the design is
              clear and effective, a website visitors like to come back to.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <IconBuild />
            <h3>Build</h3>
            <p>
              Responsive websites and web apps, built with a strong focus on
              performance. Blazing fast, so your visitors quickly find what
              they're looking for.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <IconService />
            <h3>Service</h3>
            <p>
              After delivery I do the maintenance, host your website, install
              updates and tweak the website for the best security and
              conversion.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <Cases>
        <header>
          <h2>What do I make?</h2>
          <p>
            I build custom responsive websites, from a simple one-pager to
            complete webshops. HTML, CSS and JavaScript hold no secrets for me.
            WordPress is my CMS of choice, but I have experience with plenty of
            other back-end languages and frameworks.
          </p>
          <p>
            Below is a selection of my most recent work. If you'd like to see
            more, <a href="mailto:hi@stef.co">get in touch</a>.
          </p>
        </header>
        <Case title="International startup" period="2026–now">
          <p>
            Since September 2026 I've been working on the web app of an
            international startup as a full-stack engineer, in React and
            TypeScript. I can't name them yet.
          </p>
        </Case>
        <Case title="SaaS for financial advisors" period="2026">
          <p>
            A multi-tenant platform in Laravel, with Livewire and Filament. I
            can't name the client yet. In 2026 I added features with a lot of
            business rules, including features that use AI. I built much of it
            with AI agents, with tests (Pest) and static analysis (Larastan) as
            a safety net.
          </p>
        </Case>
        <Case
          title="Nerds"
          period="2024–2025"
          url="https://nerds.nl"
          image={nerds}
        >
          <p>
            Nerds is a helpdesk for all your digital devices and services, also
            as a white-label service for other companies. As lead full-stack
            engineer I led the rebuild of their legacy PHP platform in Next.js,
            React and Tailwind. I built the front-end: a fast, keyboard-first
            interface on top of one API for several ticketing systems. I also
            introduced Scrum, mentored a junior developer and delivered a pilot
            for investors.
          </p>
        </Case>
        <Case
          title="Nexus Institute"
          period="2017–2023"
          url="https://nexus-institute.com"
          image={nexusInstituut}
        >
          <p>
            I made the Nexus Institute website responsive, so it scales with
            different screen sizes. The old website used a bespoke CMS. To loud
            cheers from the Nexus editors I moved it to WordPress. A new
            WooCommerce store lets customers order the latest Nexus magazine
            with great ease.
          </p>
        </Case>
        <Case
          title="De Speld"
          period="2018–2021"
          url="https://speld.nl"
          image={speld}
        >
          <p>
            De Speld is the largest satirical website in the Netherlands, with
            more than 1.5 million visitors a month. Over the past year I did a
            big refactor and modernised the codebase. I also developed new
            features and connected the website to a new advertising partner.
            Finally we introduced the “Vage Kennis” subscription model, which
            lets visitors become a member and see an ad-free version of the
            website.
          </p>
        </Case>
        <Case
          title="Quai des Notaires"
          period="2018–2019"
          url="https://quaidesnotaires.com"
          image={quaiDesNotaires}
        >
          <p>
            Quai des Notaires is a French startup in the notary market. I was
            project lead of a team that converted a Symfony 3 web application
            with Twig templates into a Symfony 4 GraphQL API with a React
            front-end.
          </p>
        </Case>
        <Case
          title="Hogeschool Utrecht"
          period="2018"
          url="https://pathfinder.stef.co"
          image={hogeschoolUtrecht}
        >
          <p>
            Hogeschool Utrecht asked me to develop a tool for selecting
            strategies for behaviour change. Based on the design by{" "}
            <a
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              href="https://www.panton.nl"
            >
              Panton
            </a>{" "}
            I built a responsive React progressive web app.
          </p>
        </Case>
      </Cases>

      <Contact />
    </Container>
  </Main>
</Base>
